* Current-mirror TIA, shunt feedback, passive shunt-peaking inductor - reconstruction
* LTspice: File > Open (All files) > this .net > Run.  Keep ptm90.lib in this folder.
* One analysis at a time: un-comment the one you want with ";" removed.
.include ptm90.lib
.temp 35

Vdd vdd 0 dc 1
Cpd in 0 450f
CL out 0 50f
Iin 0 in dc 0 ac 1
Ibp vbp 0 dc 20u
Mdp vbp vbp vdd vdd pmos90 W=2u L=200n AD=0.4p AS=0.4p PD=4.4u PS=4.4u
Cbp vbp vdd 2p
Mp1 in vbp vdd vdd pmos90 W=4.169u L=200n AD=0.8339p AS=0.8339p PD=8.739u PS=8.739u
M1 in in 0 0 nmos90 W=2.395u L=100n AD=0.479p AS=0.479p PD=5.19u PS=5.19u
M2 out in 0 0 nmos90 W=24.53u L=100n AD=4.907p AS=4.907p PD=49.47u PS=49.47u
Rf out in 9.011k
RL vdd lx 89.223
Lp lx out 17.843n

.ac dec 40 1Meg 100G
;.noise V(out) Iin dec 40 1Meg 100G
;.op
;Eye diagram: open the matching _eye.net file instead (transient with a PRBS7 current source).
.meas AC zt0 FIND mag(V(out)) AT 10Meg
.meas AC zpk MAX mag(V(out))
.meas AC f3db WHEN mag(V(out))=zt0/sqrt(2) FALL=1
.backanno
.end
